 ### [Diffusion-Based 3D Inpainting](14834-diffusion-based-3d-inpainting.md)
-Diffusion-Based 3D Inpainting is a method that utilizes a self-trained 2D inpainting diffusion model to reconstruct missing or masked regions in a 3D scene represented by a radiance field. It solves the problem of 3D scene completion or object removal by combining explicit reconstruction constraints for visible areas with implicit diffusion priors for occluded areas. It is distinguished from sibling methods like [Inpainting SDS Loss](11185-inpainting-sds-loss.md) by its specific reliance on a *self-trained* 2D inpainting model rather than a generic pre-trained one, and from [SKED](12268-sked.md) by its focus on distilling 2D inpainting results into a single 3D scene via iterative refinement. See [Diffusion-Based 3D Inpainting](14834-diffusion-based-3d-inpainting.md).
+Utilizes a self-trained 2D inpainting diffusion model to reconstruct missing regions by combining explicit reconstruction constraints for visible areas with implicit diffusion priors for occluded areas.
 
 ### [Reference-guided Controllable Inpainting of Neural Radiance Fields](15289-reference-guided-controllable-inpainting-of-neural-radiance-.md)
-This method performs 3D inpainting of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) by substituting a single reference view with a diffusion-generated target view, then optimizing the NeRF to match the new view while maintaining consistency with the remaining input views. It solves the problem of inserting or modifying objects in a 3D scene without requiring multi-view supervision for the target content. It differs from [Inpainting SDS Loss](11185-inpainting-sds-loss.md) by using a deterministic 2D inpainting prior (Stable Diffusion) followed by a bilateral solver for residual smoothing, rather than relying solely on gradient-based SDS guidance during optimization. See [Reference-guided Controllable Inpainting of Neural Radiance Fields](15289-reference-guided-controllable-inpainting-of-neural-radiance-.md).
+Substitutes a single reference view with a diffusion-generated target view, then optimizes the NeRF to match the new view while maintaining consistency with remaining input views, using a bilateral solver for residual smoothing.
 
 ### [Diffusion Model Preprocessing & Training Setup](15506-diffusion-model-preprocessing-training-setup.md)
-This method defines the data preprocessing pipeline and training configuration for a fine-tuned Stable Diffusion 1.5 model used as a semantic prior in Street View Synthesis (SGD). It solves the problem of adapting a 2D diffusion model to guide 3D radiance field optimization by ensuring the input data distribution matches the model's expectations and by enabling classifier-free guidance. It sets itself apart from general diffusion training by specifically addressing the aspect ratio distortion of wide-angle street view images (KITTI-360) and enforcing a perspective gap between reference and training views to improve robustness. See [Diffusion Model Preprocessing & Training Setup](15506-diffusion-model-preprocessing-training-setup.md).
