 ### Blending Refinement Model
-A model employing two Instruct-Pix2Pix processes as learned regularization to improve quality by purifying noisy mixup images and aligning them with detailed characteristics, using averaged latent codes for stability [S6]. In the first pass, the mixup image is used as input and the original image as a condition to purify the noisy mixup image by preserving structural integrity [S6]. In the second pass, the resulting image from the first pass is used as input and the mixup image as the condition to align with the mixup image’s detailed characteristics [S6]. It introduces $n_r$ noised latent codes and updates them independently, computing the average of the latent codes and decoding it back into the image [S6]. Parameters: $n_r=5$, input timestep $t=0.6$, and 3 diffusion steps [S6].
